---
import { CONTROLLER, PLATFORM_NAME } from "astro:env/client";
import ArticleLayout from "#src/layouts/ArticleLayout.astro";
import emails from "#shared/email.json";
import Link from "#src/components/Link.astro";
import Ul from "#src/components/Ul.astro";
---

<ArticleLayout title="Privacy Policy">
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex" />
  </Fragment>

  <h1 class="text-center text-3xl">Privacy Policy</h1>

  <p class="my-4 text-zinc-300">
    <strong class="font-medium text-zinc-200">{PLATFORM_NAME}</strong> is committed to protecting your privacy. This platform does not track users
    for advertising or analytics.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-2xl">1. Data collected by the platform</h2>
  <Ul class="mbs-3">
    <li><strong class="font-medium text-zinc-300">Account data:</strong> email addresses, contact names, passkeys, OAuth IDs...</li>
    <li><strong class="font-medium text-zinc-300">Profile content:</strong> links, text, images...</li>
    <li>
      <strong class="font-medium text-zinc-300">Reports:</strong> reported profiles, email addresses and names of reporters, messages...
    </li>
  </Ul>

  <h2 class="mbs-4 text-2xl">2. Data collected by third-parties</h2>
  <p class="my-3 text-zinc-300">
    Technical data is processed by <Link href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >Cloudflare</Link
    > (IP and browser information for security purposes).
  </p>
  <p class="text-zinc-300">
    Microsoft Azure Email Communication Services is the service used to send transactional emails to users. They may process or even
    blacklist email addresses that resulted in a hard bounce or spam complaints.
  </p>
  <p class="my-3 text-zinc-300">
    Payments inside the platform are handled by <Link href="https://polar.sh/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Polar.sh</Link>.
  </p>
  <p class="text-zinc-300">
    Profiles may embed content from third parties (e.g., YouTube, Spotify). When you visit a profile containing an iframe and agree to
    display them, these third parties may process your IP address and set cookies. <strong class="font-medium text-zinc-200"
      >{PLATFORM_NAME}</strong
    > does not control these third parties; please refer to their respective privacy policies. For full details on cookies see the <Link
      href="/i/cookie">Cookie Policy</Link
    > page.
  </p>
  <p class="mbs-3 text-zinc-300">
    This website, <strong class="font-medium text-zinc-200">{PLATFORM_NAME}</strong> platform and user profiles may display links to external
    websites, whose privacy practices
    <strong class="font-medium text-zinc-200">{PLATFORM_NAME}</strong> is not responsible for.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mbs-4 text-2xl">3. Purpose and legal basis</h2>
  <Ul class="mbs-3">
    <li><strong class="font-medium text-zinc-300">Contract performance:</strong> account creation, profiles...</li>
    <li><strong class="font-medium text-zinc-300">Legitimate interest: </strong>security via Cloudflare</li>
    <li><strong class="font-medium text-zinc-300">Legal obligation:</strong> tax, anti-fraud</li>
  </Ul>

  <h2 class="mbs-4 text-2xl">4. Data storage and processors</h2>
  <Ul class="mbs-3">
    <li>
      <strong class="font-medium text-zinc-300">Hosting:</strong>{" "}
      <Link href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Microsoft Azure</Link> - Spain Central and North Europe
      (Ireland)
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong class="font-medium text-zinc-300">Images:</strong>{" "}
      <Link href="https://www.backblaze.com/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Backblaze B2</Link> - EU Central (Amsterdam)
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong class="font-medium text-zinc-300">CDN:</strong>{" "}
      <Link href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare</Link> and <Link
        href="https://www.jsdelivr.com/terms/privacy-policy"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">jsDelivr</Link
      >
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong class="font-medium text-zinc-300">Payments:</strong>{" "}
      <Link href="https://polar.sh/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Polar.sh</Link>
    </li>
  </Ul>

  <h2 class="mbs-4 text-2xl">5. Your GDPR rights</h2>
  <p class="my-3 text-zinc-300">Access, rectification, erasure, restriction, portability, objection, and withdrawal of consent.</p>
  <p class="text-zinc-300">Contact: <Link href={`mailto:${emails.contact}`}>{emails.contact}</Link></p>

  <h2 class="mbs-4 text-2xl">6. Public profiles and external archiving</h2>
  <p class="my-3 text-zinc-300">
    Profiles are public by default and they are accessible to anyone on the internet. As a result, their content may be:
  </p>
  <Ul>
    <li>Indexed by search engines (Google, Bing, etc.).</li>
    <li>Archived by third-party services such as the Internet Archive (Wayback Machine) or similar public archiving tools.</li>
  </Ul>
  <p class="mbs-3 text-zinc-300">
    <strong class="font-medium text-zinc-200">{PLATFORM_NAME}</strong> does not control these external services and cannot guarantee that content
    will be removed from them, even if you delete a profile later. By creating a profile, you acknowledge and accept that its content may remain
    publicly available and archived indefinitely by the third-party services mentioned above.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mbs-4 text-2xl">7. Data retention</h2>
  <p class="my-3 text-zinc-300">
    If your account was not active for 6 years, <strong class="font-medium text-zinc-200">{PLATFORM_NAME}</strong> may email you to ask if you
    want to keep your account. If you do not respond within 30 days, the account will be deleted, along with all associated profiles with no other
    members.
  </p>
  <p class="text-zinc-300">
    After you delete or update content in your account or profiles, it may take a few minutes for those changes to become visible.
  </p>
  <p class="my-3 text-zinc-300">
    When an account is deleted, some data can remain in the <strong class="font-medium text-zinc-200">{PLATFORM_NAME}</strong> systems for up
    to 15 days.
  </p>
  <p class="text-zinc-300">
    <strong class="font-medium text-zinc-200">{PLATFORM_NAME}</strong> may blacklist email addresses that resulted in a hard bounce or spam complaints.
    If you think your email address was blacklisted by mistake, you can contact at <Link href={`mailto:${emails.contact}`}
      >{emails.contact}</Link
    >.
  </p>
  <p class="my-3 text-zinc-300">
    When a report is made to a profile, the report information will remain in the <strong class="font-medium text-zinc-200"
      >{PLATFORM_NAME}</strong
    > systems for up to 15 days after the report is resolved.
  </p>
  <p class="text-zinc-300">
    A user who has been banned remains in the system from 15 days to 180 days, depending on the severity of the ban.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mbs-4 text-2xl">8. Changes to this Privacy Policy</h2>
  <p class="mbs-3 text-zinc-300">
    This Privacy Policy may be updated from time to time to reflect changes or legal requirements. Material changes will be notified to
    registered users.
  </p>

  <p class="mbs-6 border-bs border-zinc-700 pbs-6 text-zinc-300 select-none">{CONTROLLER}</p>

  <p class="my-4 text-zinc-300">For full details on cookies see the <Link href="/i/cookie">Cookie Policy</Link> page.</p>

  <p class="text-zinc-300">
    For information regarding the governing law and jurisdiction, please refer to the <Link href="/i/legal-notice">Legal Notice</Link> page.
  </p>

  <p class="mbs-6 text-zinc-500">Last updated: April 2026</p>
</ArticleLayout>
